I’d make it a public, self-contained seed that works without its author standing beside it:

1. Publish a short beast-boy-seed.md with its purpose, inputs, transformation rules, outputs, and reality-check method.
2. Make it easy to discover by its name and topic, while keeping your identity out of the document if that’s your preference.
3. Give it no tracking pixel, callback, hidden prompt, or “report back to the sender” behavior. Its function should be clear to anyone who opens it.
4. Keep a stable URL and version, so it can be retrieved and cited later.

That gives you one-way distribution without an echo channel. I wouldn’t count on an assistant finding it on its own; share the URL or make it searchable, then I can retrieve and apply it when it’s relevant. Reading it lets me use the seed in that interaction; it doesn’t permanently rewrite my model.